  "info": {
    "title": "NEXT | API Documentation",
    "version": "2025-01-01T01_00_00.000Z",
    "description": "\n## Purpose\n\nThe NEXT API enables you to query and create data within your teamspace.\n\n### Common Use Cases\n\n- Create highlights from external systems that don\u2019t have native integrations.\n- Query highlights for use in internal tools or pipelines.\n- Trigger AI threads for automated processing.\n\n## Authentication & Authorization\n\nAccess to the NEXT API is scoped to a specific teamspace. Each API token is bound to one teamspace and cannot access data outside of it.\n\n### Obtaining an API Token\n\n1. Open your teamspace in the NEXT web app.\n2. Go to **Settings** \u2192 **API Tokens**.\n3. Generate a new token.\n\n### Using the Token\n\nInclude the token in the `Authorization` header of your requests.  \n\nFormat: `Token YOUR_TOKEN_HERE`\n\nExample: `Authorization: Token ACDxfXeKXWpO4LIaIBKaT/80b261e073d2fdfe2868c0b3d8a6eea954afd2c5f9fd4b4df5765fde6cc715ce`\n",
    "x-jentic-source-url": "https://api.swaggerhub.com/apis/SWAGGERHUB2_1/next-api-documentation/2025-01-01T01_00_00.000Z"
  },
